        "outline_action_recovered_by_policy": false,
        "remaining_gap": "The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.",
        "remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy": false,
        "status": "unmet",
        "useful_material": "The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies."
      },
